1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,503
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,586 --> 00:00:05,046
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,385
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,468 --> 00:00:12,721
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,804 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,476
[muffled shrieking]

7
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:20,311
[Mongki] <i>They're secured, boss.</i>

8
00:00:20,395 --> 00:00:22,564
I made sure they're sleeping soundly.

9
00:00:22,647 --> 00:00:24,023
Bro, they're going to kill me.

10
00:00:24,107 --> 00:00:25,567
- [Jona squeals]
- [gunshot]

11
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:26,735
[gunfire blasting]

12
00:00:26,818 --> 00:00:29,612
[Emerson] <i>What do you want?</i>
<i>Burn alive here or get shot outside?!</i>

13
00:00:29,696 --> 00:00:31,865
[Olga] <i>Can you take the child from me?</i>

14
00:00:31,948 --> 00:00:35,368
I'm annoyed with her. She's too nosy.

15
00:00:35,452 --> 00:00:37,662
We'll tell you when to return the child.

16
00:00:37,746 --> 00:00:39,664
[Martina, in English] <i>So,</i>
<i>just deal with her. Okay?</i>

17
00:00:39,748 --> 00:00:40,623
[Paldo] Ouch!

18
00:00:40,707 --> 00:00:42,625
- [screaming and panicking]
- It's Brother Paldo!

19
00:00:42,709 --> 00:00:45,044
[firetruck siren wailing]

20
00:00:45,128 --> 00:00:47,046
[Ibyang] <i>Just give me back to Tatoy!</i>

21
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:49,132
You're a bad mother!

22
00:00:49,215 --> 00:00:50,550
I'm not a bad mother!

23
00:00:50,633 --> 00:00:51,676
[squeals]

24
00:00:54,054 --> 00:00:55,555
Mama!

25
00:00:56,139 --> 00:00:57,432
[Mona] <i>You look like Adamus.</i>

26
00:00:57,515 --> 00:00:59,184
The guardian of the water gem

27
00:00:59,267 --> 00:01:00,727
- in <i>Encantadia</i>!
- Oh, yes!

28
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:02,270
He's too handsome compared to me.

29
00:01:02,353 --> 00:01:04,481
[Olga] <i>I thought you</i>
<i>didn't want me anymore</i>

30
00:01:04,564 --> 00:01:05,899
<i>because I'm a bad mother.</i>

31
00:01:05,982 --> 00:01:10,737
I'm here because you are my mama.

32
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:14,115
I won't be naughty and stubborn anymore.

33
00:01:14,199 --> 00:01:15,617
[Ibyang, in English] <i>Good night, Ma.</i>

34
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:16,868
[in English] Good night, Ibyang.

35
00:01:16,951 --> 00:01:18,161
[sniffles]

36
00:01:18,244 --> 00:01:19,120
[softly] Go on.

37
00:01:19,662 --> 00:01:21,206
Careful on the stairs, okay?

38
00:01:21,289 --> 00:01:22,373
Yes.

39
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:26,336
PREVIOUSLY

40
00:01:26,419 --> 00:01:28,630
[music swells]

41
00:01:30,507 --> 00:01:31,674
[music fades]

42
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:33,301
[Charmi] What happened, friend?

43
00:01:33,384 --> 00:01:36,221
Why does it seem like
you're treating the kid differently?

44
00:01:37,388 --> 00:01:38,223
Huh?

45
00:01:39,224 --> 00:01:42,227
And it's like… Wow.
Why, oh, fantastic, marvelous!

46
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:44,604
You even cleaned your house.

47
00:01:44,687 --> 00:01:47,106
Are you sure you didn't hit your head?

48
00:01:47,774 --> 00:01:48,817
Oh, want to test it?

49
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:51,361
Let's roll down the stairs together.
You want to?

50
00:01:51,444 --> 00:01:53,279
Come on. Can't you take a joke?

51
00:01:53,363 --> 00:01:54,489
- Come on.
- Hm-mm.

52
00:01:54,572 --> 00:01:56,407
But you know, in fairness to Ibyang,

53
00:01:57,242 --> 00:01:59,619
she's sweet and thoughtful.

54
00:02:00,829 --> 00:02:04,457
Whoever her parents are,
they're very lucky.

55
00:02:04,541 --> 00:02:06,251
[gentle music playing]

56
00:02:06,334 --> 00:02:07,961
With everything she's been through,

57
00:02:08,044 --> 00:02:09,337
she's still a good child.

58
00:02:10,171 --> 00:02:11,923
It's not hard to love her.

59
00:02:14,384 --> 00:02:15,426
Oh. Aw!

60
00:02:16,219 --> 00:02:18,263
See, that's it.

61
00:02:18,346 --> 00:02:21,641
Why don't you take
being a mother to Ibyang seriously?

62
00:02:21,724 --> 00:02:28,231
Maybe this is the universe's way of giving
you another chance at motherhood.

63
00:02:30,483 --> 00:02:31,317
Oh.

64
00:02:31,401 --> 00:02:33,611
[phone ringing]

65
00:02:33,695 --> 00:02:35,572
Hey! It's Madam.

66
00:02:35,655 --> 00:02:37,157
Go. I'll take it.

67
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:38,324
Take this.

68
00:02:38,408 --> 00:02:40,577
[mysterious music playing]

69
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:42,036
Hello, Madam?

70
00:02:43,246 --> 00:02:44,914
Why did you take so long to answer?

71
00:02:44,998 --> 00:02:47,083
Well, you didn't show up.

72
00:02:47,876 --> 00:02:49,002
[smirks]

73
00:02:50,461 --> 00:02:51,880
What did you say?

74
00:02:51,963 --> 00:02:54,048
[titters] Oh, sorry.

75
00:02:54,716 --> 00:02:56,301
Madam, I was just busy.

76
00:02:56,384 --> 00:02:58,636
Okay. So, you said you don't want
Ibyang anymore.

77
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:00,305
[in English] Well, that's great news.

78
00:03:00,388 --> 00:03:03,224
I think it's time
you give the child back to us.

79
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:05,351
Right away?

80
00:03:06,311 --> 00:03:08,396
Why? Is there a problem?

81
00:03:09,647 --> 00:03:10,565
[in English] Don't worry.

82
00:03:11,232 --> 00:03:13,484
[in English] You'll have
200,000 pesos bonus.

83
00:03:13,568 --> 00:03:15,153
[in English] I will text you
where we'll meet.

84
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:18,948
Why? Are you returning her
to her real mother?

85
00:03:19,532 --> 00:03:20,950
[in English] That's none of your concern.

86
00:03:21,034 --> 00:03:22,243
[in English] Just wait for my text.

87
00:03:23,036 --> 00:03:24,412
Okay.

88
00:03:24,495 --> 00:03:28,291
[rousing music playing]

89
00:03:29,250 --> 00:03:31,294
[suave theme music playing]

90
00:03:34,213 --> 00:03:36,049
[motorcycle revving]

91
00:03:36,132 --> 00:03:37,008
[sewing machine whirring]

92
00:03:37,091 --> 00:03:37,967
[scratches]

93
00:03:38,051 --> 00:03:38,927
[snipping]

94
00:03:40,053 --> 00:03:44,641
[sewing machine clacking]

95
00:03:44,724 --> 00:03:45,975
[gunshots]

96
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:49,520
[clicking]

97
00:03:49,604 --> 00:03:50,939
[snipping]

98
00:03:52,148 --> 00:03:53,441
[electronic blipping]

99
00:03:57,612 --> 00:03:58,780
[music fades]

100
00:03:58,863 --> 00:04:00,531
I'm part of the intelligence unit

101
00:04:00,615 --> 00:04:05,578
conducting the investigation
into the commotion that happened here.

102
00:04:06,663 --> 00:04:12,418
Any information you can give me
regarding the culprits?

103
00:04:13,086 --> 00:04:15,630
Two of our men saw them.

104
00:04:16,464 --> 00:04:22,303
The armed men who stormed in here
were speaking Russian.

105
00:04:22,387 --> 00:04:25,431
[pensive music playing]

106
00:04:25,515 --> 00:04:29,269
They took Lily, our godchild.

107
00:04:29,769 --> 00:04:30,812
[scoffs]

108
00:04:30,895 --> 00:04:31,896
[in English] I'm so sorry.

109
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:37,318
Anything else your men saw?

110
00:04:37,402 --> 00:04:42,490
They grabbed one man.
One of the tribal dancers.

111
00:04:43,074 --> 00:04:45,618
They said he fought well.

112
00:04:45,702 --> 00:04:50,123
[in English] And I just don't know
why they captured him along with Lily.

113
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:54,669
[in English] But one of my guards said
he was trying to protect Lily.

114
00:04:55,920 --> 00:05:00,633
Do you think the people
looking for Lily are involved?

115
00:05:00,717 --> 00:05:03,052
She never told me about it.

116
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:06,848
All I know is she's scared

117
00:05:06,931 --> 00:05:11,311
and feels hounded
by people she won't name.

118
00:05:12,687 --> 00:05:15,398
[music fades]

119
00:05:16,232 --> 00:05:18,026
- [thumps]
- [in English] Talk!

120
00:05:18,818 --> 00:05:22,405
- [in English] Or you will be…
- [grunts]

121
00:05:24,949 --> 00:05:26,659
our punching bag.

122
00:05:26,743 --> 00:05:29,871
- [in English] Every day and every night!
- [Lily whimpers]

123
00:05:29,954 --> 00:05:31,956
[ominous music playing]

124
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:34,500
[in English] I think
this will make him talk.

125
00:05:36,002 --> 00:05:36,836
[Samir in Russian] Stop it!

126
00:05:36,919 --> 00:05:38,046
[Samir applauds]

127
00:05:38,129 --> 00:05:39,547
[in English] That is enough.
That is enough.

128
00:05:41,883 --> 00:05:43,092
[in English] Hello!

129
00:05:44,969 --> 00:05:46,929
[in English] So, you're not going to talk.

130
00:05:48,681 --> 00:05:50,850
[in English] You're not going to say
where the laptop is.

131
00:05:52,143 --> 00:05:53,186
[sighs]

132
00:05:55,605 --> 00:05:56,814
[in English] No.

133
00:05:57,857 --> 00:05:59,776
[in English] I will make you talk.

134
00:06:00,902 --> 00:06:05,364
[in English] You see,
men like you have a family.

135
00:06:07,492 --> 00:06:09,118
[in English] Maybe you have a wife.

136
00:06:11,245 --> 00:06:14,373
[in English] Maybe you have
a son or a daughter.

137
00:06:15,583 --> 00:06:17,126
[in English] Maybe a dog.

138
00:06:17,210 --> 00:06:22,799
[pensive music playing]

139
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:27,428
[in English] I have men right now

140
00:06:27,512 --> 00:06:31,057
searching for all of your beloved.

141
00:06:31,140 --> 00:06:33,059
[in English] And when they find them,

142
00:06:34,143 --> 00:06:37,563
they will bring them back here,

143
00:06:37,647 --> 00:06:39,107
and I will kill

144
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:42,568
every one of them
right in front of your face.

145
00:06:44,445 --> 00:06:48,783
[in English] Or you can tell me
who you work for

146
00:06:48,866 --> 00:06:51,327
and where my laptop is.

147
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:08,010
[phone rings]

148
00:07:08,094 --> 00:07:09,720
[music swells]

149
00:07:09,804 --> 00:07:11,431
[in English] Update me.

150
00:07:13,975 --> 00:07:17,895
[tense music playing]

151
00:07:19,564 --> 00:07:20,731
[in English] Mission status.

152
00:07:21,816 --> 00:07:23,734
[in English] Outside the establishment.

153
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:27,738
[in English] Potential headquarters
of Anthony "Atoy" Padua.

154
00:08:08,905 --> 00:08:10,781
[in English] You're just
wasting your time.

155
00:08:10,865 --> 00:08:12,325
[ominous music playing]

156
00:08:12,408 --> 00:08:13,826
[in English] I have no family.

157
00:08:14,410 --> 00:08:16,871
[in English] Everyone has a weakness,

158
00:08:16,954 --> 00:08:18,831
and I will find yours,

159
00:08:18,915 --> 00:08:22,502
and you will regret everything.

160
00:08:28,049 --> 00:08:29,967
[in English] There's nothing
that can hurt me.

161
00:08:30,927 --> 00:08:32,011
[in English] Nothing.

162
00:08:33,679 --> 00:08:35,556
[in English] Is that so, mister?

163
00:08:43,397 --> 00:08:44,857
[clicks]

164
00:08:44,941 --> 00:08:46,108
[music swells]

165
00:08:46,192 --> 00:08:47,276
[grunts]

166
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:49,153
‪[sighs, gasps]

167
00:08:49,237 --> 00:08:51,239
[in English] How about that? Hmm?

168
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:53,574
- [in English] How about that?
- [groans]

169
00:08:54,867 --> 00:08:57,328
[in English] Stop! No! No, no.

170
00:08:58,287 --> 00:09:00,206
[whimpering]

171
00:09:01,332 --> 00:09:02,375
[Samir, in English] Well…

172
00:09:08,756 --> 00:09:10,258
[in English] What about this one? Hmm?

173
00:09:11,217 --> 00:09:13,177
[in English] Is she important to you?

174
00:09:13,261 --> 00:09:14,345
[in English] Does she matter to you?

175
00:09:16,305 --> 00:09:18,182
[Atoy, in English] No, no, no! Stop! Stop!

176
00:09:18,266 --> 00:09:19,725
[music intensifies]

177
00:09:20,434 --> 00:09:24,647
[in English] If you kill me now, you will
never be able to open that laptop.

178
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:29,902
[in English] The ambassador
has all the passwords.

179
00:09:30,653 --> 00:09:32,572
[in English] But it changes every 30 days.

180
00:09:33,656 --> 00:09:35,116
[in English] How would you know the code?

181
00:09:35,866 --> 00:09:37,952
[in English] I'm the only one
who can access it,

182
00:09:38,035 --> 00:09:41,581
and I can erase every classified info
you have on there.

183
00:09:43,332 --> 00:09:44,667
[in English] You know you need me.

184
00:09:46,836 --> 00:09:48,963
[in English] That plan
didn't work out, huh?

185
00:09:49,046 --> 00:09:51,007
[cackles]

186
00:09:51,090 --> 00:09:53,342
[grunts]

187
00:09:53,426 --> 00:09:54,343
[grunts]

188
00:09:57,722 --> 00:09:58,556
[Audrey grunting]

189
00:09:58,639 --> 00:09:59,807
[Janine whimpering]

190
00:09:59,890 --> 00:10:01,309
[suspicious music playing]

191
00:10:01,976 --> 00:10:04,770
[muffled mumbling]

192
00:10:05,271 --> 00:10:07,440
[gasps] Child, untie me.

193
00:10:07,523 --> 00:10:09,150
Quick, faster. Hurry.

194
00:10:09,233 --> 00:10:10,568
Child, child…

195
00:10:10,651 --> 00:10:12,236
- [Janine groans]
- [Audrey shrieks]

196
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:13,195
[Janine shrieks]

197
00:10:13,279 --> 00:10:15,156
- You're trying to escape?
- [Audrey] What? What will you do to her?!

198
00:10:15,239 --> 00:10:16,949
- You're escaping?!
- [Audrey] Oh, don't hurt her! Red!

199
00:10:17,033 --> 00:10:18,200
Take her!

200
00:10:18,284 --> 00:10:19,910
- No!
- Let me go! Mommy!

201
00:10:19,994 --> 00:10:21,787
- Let go of my child!
- [Janine squeals]

202
00:10:21,871 --> 00:10:23,205
Release her!

203
00:10:23,914 --> 00:10:24,790
[in English] No!

204
00:10:25,708 --> 00:10:27,460
[groans]

205
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:28,836
[ominous music playing]

206
00:10:31,714 --> 00:10:33,924
- [Audrey sobs]
- [sighs]

207
00:10:34,592 --> 00:10:36,344
Oh, Audrey.

208
00:10:36,427 --> 00:10:38,387
[sobs]

209
00:10:38,471 --> 00:10:40,848
You can't coax anyone here anymore.

210
00:10:40,931 --> 00:10:42,808
Daddy isn't here to help you either.

211
00:10:42,892 --> 00:10:44,435
[Audrey sobs]

212
00:10:44,518 --> 00:10:47,772
So, if you want to live longer,
learn to listen to me.

213
00:10:48,522 --> 00:10:50,066
[in English] You understand?

214
00:10:50,149 --> 00:10:50,983
Huh?

215
00:10:51,567 --> 00:10:52,902
[in English] Yes?

216
00:10:52,985 --> 00:10:56,238
[music intensifies]

217
00:11:04,789 --> 00:11:06,582
- [foreboding music playing]
- [heavy breathing]

218
00:11:11,712 --> 00:11:12,546
- [Janine] Grandpa.
- Janine?

219
00:11:13,297 --> 00:11:14,715
[panting]

220
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:16,300
- [in English] Are you alright?
- Grandpa, Uncle Red

221
00:11:16,384 --> 00:11:17,676
locked me and Mommy up.

222
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:19,512
[Janine] We were supposed
to leave for the US,

223
00:11:19,595 --> 00:11:21,389
but Uncle Red stopped us.

224
00:11:21,472 --> 00:11:24,100
Then he locked us up,
and now they took me.

225
00:11:24,183 --> 00:11:26,852
I don't know
where they're taking me, Grandpa.

226
00:11:26,936 --> 00:11:28,187
[mutters]

227
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:31,190
[in English] Okay, okay.
Janine, go on ahead.

228
00:11:31,273 --> 00:11:33,067
[in English] Go to the garage. Okay?

229
00:11:33,150 --> 00:11:35,111
Grandpa, save Mommy.

230
00:11:35,194 --> 00:11:36,028
[in English] I will. Go!

231
00:11:36,112 --> 00:11:37,113
[in English] Now.

232
00:11:41,492 --> 00:11:43,536
Dad, you shouldn't have let Janine escape.

233
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:47,289
What did you do to Audrey,
to my granddaughter?!

234
00:11:47,373 --> 00:11:48,624
[pensive music playing]

235
00:11:48,707 --> 00:11:50,126
She's not really your granddaughter.

236
00:11:50,876 --> 00:11:52,545
She's not really Audrey's daughter either.

237
00:11:52,628 --> 00:11:55,673
[tense music playing]

238
00:12:05,808 --> 00:12:09,728
[suspicious music playing]

239
00:12:09,812 --> 00:12:10,646
[grunts]

240
00:12:16,777 --> 00:12:18,028
[grunting]

241
00:12:20,531 --> 00:12:22,616
[grunts, panting]

242
00:12:24,702 --> 00:12:25,578
[grunts]

243
00:12:28,664 --> 00:12:31,208
[pensive music playing]

244
00:12:33,002 --> 00:12:36,464
[grunts, panting]

245
00:12:37,965 --> 00:12:39,467
[grunts, panting]

246
00:12:45,264 --> 00:12:46,348
[grunting]

247
00:12:48,434 --> 00:12:49,560
[panting]

248
00:12:51,228 --> 00:12:53,481
[softly] Hurry, hurry.

249
00:13:01,447 --> 00:13:04,241
[grunts, panting]

250
00:13:19,798 --> 00:13:20,633
‪[grunts, panting]

251
00:13:25,763 --> 00:13:28,015
[music fades]

252
00:13:28,098 --> 00:13:29,934
[tense music playing]

253
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:35,773
[moans]

254
00:13:38,901 --> 00:13:40,194
[sighs]

255
00:13:42,112 --> 00:13:44,365
[sighing]

256
00:14:10,224 --> 00:14:11,141
[music fades]

257
00:14:11,725 --> 00:14:13,352
She's not really our blood.

258
00:14:13,435 --> 00:14:15,813
What nonsense are you saying, Red?!

259
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:17,231
[in English] It's simple. Okay?

260
00:14:18,148 --> 00:14:20,734
[in English] Martina and I
faked everything.

261
00:14:20,818 --> 00:14:22,278
[in English] Documents, papers, all of it.

262
00:14:22,361 --> 00:14:24,989
Even the people we talked to,
they were all in on it.

263
00:14:25,072 --> 00:14:29,577
So we could show Audrey
that we found her missing child.

264
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:30,494
[in English] Okay?

265
00:14:30,578 --> 00:14:32,121
So, you deceived me too?

266
00:14:32,746 --> 00:14:33,581
Why?!

267
00:14:33,664 --> 00:14:35,082
So you'd… So you'd stop!

268
00:14:35,958 --> 00:14:37,501
You kept pressuring us!

269
00:14:38,043 --> 00:14:40,337
You're always thinking about Audrey!
Audrey can't be angry,

270
00:14:40,421 --> 00:14:42,172
Audrey can't be sad!

271
00:14:42,256 --> 00:14:45,384
You don't understand.
Your daughter is manipulating you!

272
00:14:45,467 --> 00:14:47,678
You're becoming a fool
because you kept protecting Audrey!

273
00:14:47,761 --> 00:14:49,471
You're really worthless.

274
00:14:49,555 --> 00:14:51,307
[grunting and groaning]

275
00:14:52,016 --> 00:14:54,602
[thumping and thudding]

276
00:14:54,685 --> 00:14:58,939
[tense music playing]

277
00:14:59,523 --> 00:15:00,482
[softly] So?

278
00:15:01,609 --> 00:15:02,693
You'll shoot me?

279
00:15:03,527 --> 00:15:05,029
You'll shoot me because of Audrey?

280
00:15:10,075 --> 00:15:11,785
- [music fades]
- [sighs]

281
00:15:13,329 --> 00:15:16,498
[suspicious music playing]

282
00:15:24,423 --> 00:15:26,050
[huffs]

283
00:15:27,968 --> 00:15:30,512
[rousing music playing]

284
00:16:17,434 --> 00:16:19,395
[music fades]

285
00:16:19,478 --> 00:16:22,439
[tense music playing]

286
00:16:24,316 --> 00:16:25,943
[sighs]

287
00:16:26,026 --> 00:16:29,321
[sighs]

288
00:16:31,573 --> 00:16:32,408
‪[grunts]

289
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,385
[whimpering]

290
00:16:52,886 --> 00:16:56,056
[sinister music playing]

291
00:16:57,474 --> 00:16:58,934
[whimpering]

292
00:17:08,944 --> 00:17:10,696
Where is Audrey?

293
00:17:10,779 --> 00:17:12,573
Bring Audrey out!

294
00:17:14,074 --> 00:17:17,244
Go! Shoot me. Go ahead.

295
00:17:17,953 --> 00:17:19,663
[in English] Don't push me, Red.

296
00:17:19,747 --> 00:17:21,331
[in English] Don't push me!

297
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:31,175
‪[soft gasping]

298
00:17:39,266 --> 00:17:40,350
Admit it.

299
00:17:40,434 --> 00:17:41,351
[music fades]

300
00:17:41,435 --> 00:17:43,353
You'll still side with Audrey, won't you?

301
00:17:44,521 --> 00:17:47,691
Do you know, she was going
to report us to the police?!

302
00:17:47,775 --> 00:17:49,068
I just stopped her!

303
00:17:49,151 --> 00:17:52,446
That's not a reason to lock her up.

304
00:17:52,529 --> 00:17:54,323
I know you've long wanted her gone!

305
00:17:54,406 --> 00:17:55,616
[in English] Yes!

306
00:17:55,699 --> 00:17:56,784
For a long time!

307
00:17:57,618 --> 00:17:59,745
Because she's the only one
you see, right?!

308
00:17:59,828 --> 00:18:01,205
What about me, huh?

309
00:18:01,830 --> 00:18:02,664
Did you ever treat me like your son?

310
00:18:02,748 --> 00:18:03,916
No, right?!

311
00:18:03,999 --> 00:18:05,626
Do you know why?

312
00:18:05,709 --> 00:18:06,794
[pensive music playing]

313
00:18:06,877 --> 00:18:08,504
Do you know why?!

314
00:18:08,587 --> 00:18:10,672
[music intensifies]

315
00:18:12,341 --> 00:18:13,509
What are you proud of?

316
00:18:13,592 --> 00:18:14,718
Your being out of control?!

317
00:18:14,802 --> 00:18:15,969
[in English] Dmitri, enough!

318
00:18:16,595 --> 00:18:18,597
[in English] Red, Red, stop. Don't leave!

319
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:20,390
Son, you've been drinking.

320
00:18:20,474 --> 00:18:22,351
Let's go inside, please!

321
00:18:22,434 --> 00:18:23,393
For what, Ma?

322
00:18:24,019 --> 00:18:25,646
So he can beat me up again?!

323
00:18:25,729 --> 00:18:26,605
[Dmitri] Let him go!

324
00:18:26,688 --> 00:18:29,316
He only brings us headaches!

325
00:18:29,399 --> 00:18:30,859
[in English] I've had it with him!

326
00:18:30,943 --> 00:18:32,903
[in English] Okay, fine!

327
00:18:36,281 --> 00:18:37,574
[music fades]

328
00:18:37,658 --> 00:18:38,992
I already told you, didn't I?

329
00:18:39,076 --> 00:18:40,369
[in English] I told you to stop!

330
00:18:40,452 --> 00:18:43,288
[in English] Hon. Just let him go.

331
00:18:43,372 --> 00:18:46,917
- Don't waste your effort. Just let him go!
- [in English] No!

332
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:51,421
- Hon.
- [car engine starts]

333
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:53,132
Hon. Hon!

334
00:18:58,887 --> 00:18:59,721
Get in.

335
00:19:05,561 --> 00:19:06,645
[music fades]

336
00:19:07,938 --> 00:19:10,732
[screams] I'm always the one at fault!

337
00:19:10,816 --> 00:19:13,110
[car revving]

338
00:19:16,780 --> 00:19:22,244
[car revving]

339
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:24,913
[ominous music playing]

340
00:19:26,039 --> 00:19:28,167
- [horn honks]
- [tires screeching]

341
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:29,918
[car crashes]

342
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:31,753
[tires screeching]

343
00:19:31,837 --> 00:19:33,297
[in English] Mom. Mom!

344
00:19:35,174 --> 00:19:36,258
[in English] Mommy.

345
00:19:36,967 --> 00:19:38,844
[thunder rumbling]

346
00:19:41,388 --> 00:19:42,973
[rain spattering]

347
00:19:44,933 --> 00:19:47,394
- [in English] Mom, Mom!
- [epic music playing]

348
00:19:47,477 --> 00:19:50,272
[in English] Mom! Mom, Mom, Mom…

349
00:19:50,355 --> 00:19:52,900
Help! Help!

350
00:19:52,983 --> 00:19:55,652
[in English] Mom, Mom, Mom…

351
00:19:55,736 --> 00:19:57,112
[tires screeching]

352
00:19:59,531 --> 00:20:00,407
[Red] Help!

353
00:20:01,325 --> 00:20:02,201
Help!

354
00:20:03,952 --> 00:20:05,996
[Dmitri] Hon! Hon!

355
00:20:06,788 --> 00:20:11,627
- Hon! Go! Call an ambulance!
- Mom!

356
00:20:11,710 --> 00:20:13,128
[Dmitri] Hon!

357
00:20:13,212 --> 00:20:14,129
[Red bawls]

358
00:20:14,213 --> 00:20:15,881
- Hon!
- [Red, in English] Mom, please!

359
00:20:18,467 --> 00:20:21,053
- [Dmitri] Hon. Hon. Hon!
- [indistinct]

360
00:20:21,136 --> 00:20:22,221
Hon, no!

361
00:20:22,304 --> 00:20:23,138
Hon!

362
00:20:23,222 --> 00:20:25,974
[in English] Mom, please!
Please wake up, Mom!

363
00:20:26,850 --> 00:20:29,353
[Smitri] Get out of here!

364
00:20:29,436 --> 00:20:30,395
[music fades]

365
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:34,691
[in English] I lost my wife,
your mother, because of you!

366
00:20:35,442 --> 00:20:38,153
But I still accepted you as my son.

367
00:20:38,987 --> 00:20:40,906
I knew my responsibility to you,

368
00:20:41,531 --> 00:20:43,033
and I fulfilled it,

369
00:20:43,659 --> 00:20:44,534
despite everything!

370
00:20:44,618 --> 00:20:45,953
But you never forgave me!

371
00:20:46,036 --> 00:20:47,246
[Dmitri] You're right!

372
00:20:47,996 --> 00:20:49,331
You're right!

373
00:20:49,414 --> 00:20:50,666
[melancholic music playing]

374
00:20:50,749 --> 00:20:54,753
Every goddamn day,
I wish it was you who died,

375
00:20:54,836 --> 00:20:56,171
not your mom!

376
00:20:57,047 --> 00:20:59,591
She and Audrey,

377
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:01,843
they're the only ones who matter to me.

378
00:21:03,762 --> 00:21:05,264
[music fades]

379
00:21:06,390 --> 00:21:09,101
[tense music playing]

380
00:21:11,937 --> 00:21:14,940
[panting]

381
00:21:20,362 --> 00:21:21,363
Audrey!

382
00:21:24,491 --> 00:21:25,492
[grunts]

383
00:21:26,952 --> 00:21:28,912
[groans]

384
00:21:28,996 --> 00:21:30,038
[somber music playing]

385
00:21:30,122 --> 00:21:32,457
[in English] You're going
to shut your mouth now?

386
00:21:32,541 --> 00:21:33,667
[groans]

387
00:21:33,750 --> 00:21:35,168
[groans]

388
00:21:35,252 --> 00:21:36,420
[in English] Is that it, huh?

389
00:21:36,503 --> 00:21:37,462
[smirks]

390
00:21:37,546 --> 00:21:39,172
[in English] I didn't feel a thing.

391
00:21:39,256 --> 00:21:40,215
[smirks]

392
00:21:41,216 --> 00:21:43,302
[cackles]

393
00:21:43,385 --> 00:21:45,846
[in English] You're going
to get it, sir. Oh yes.

394
00:21:45,929 --> 00:21:48,473
[cackles]

395
00:21:48,557 --> 00:21:50,017
[in English] One more, huh?

396
00:21:50,559 --> 00:21:51,393
- [grunts]
- [Lily wails]

397
00:21:51,476 --> 00:21:53,729
- [groaning]
- That's enough!

398
00:21:53,812 --> 00:21:54,938
[Atoy coughs]

399
00:21:57,024 --> 00:21:58,400
[cackles]

400
00:21:59,651 --> 00:22:01,278
[in English] You think you're tough…

401
00:22:02,195 --> 00:22:04,823
for beating up a tied-up man?

402
00:22:04,906 --> 00:22:06,074
[pensive music playing]

403
00:22:06,158 --> 00:22:08,410
[in English] You're weak, huh?

404
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:10,871
[in English] You're weak.

405
00:22:14,207 --> 00:22:16,585
[in English] You coward.

406
00:22:16,668 --> 00:22:19,212
Co… ward!

407
00:22:20,505 --> 00:22:21,673
Co… ward!

408
00:22:22,382 --> 00:22:25,552
[in English] You Zahranians are weak.

409
00:22:26,511 --> 00:22:28,805
[Atoy, in English] Cowards, huh?

410
00:22:28,889 --> 00:22:30,432
[in English] Do you know what "coward" is?

411
00:22:31,558 --> 00:22:32,851
[in English] Come here.

412
00:22:35,187 --> 00:22:39,399
[imitates a chicken clucking sound]

413
00:22:39,483 --> 00:22:40,442
[cackles]

414
00:22:41,026 --> 00:22:42,319
[in English] Release him!

415
00:22:42,402 --> 00:22:43,445
[in English] Release him now!

416
00:22:43,528 --> 00:22:45,989
[in English] I'm going
to teach this man a lesson!

417
00:22:46,073 --> 00:22:48,033
[in English] Hurry, hurry!
Release him now!

418
00:22:48,116 --> 00:22:50,911
[imitates a chicken clucking sound]

419
00:22:51,578 --> 00:22:52,454
[Atoy whoops]

420
00:22:52,537 --> 00:22:55,332
[in English] I'm going to teach you
something, sir, huh.

421
00:22:55,415 --> 00:22:59,628
[in English] You will regret this
for the rest of your life!

422
00:22:59,711 --> 00:23:01,713
[Atoy cackles]

423
00:23:01,797 --> 00:23:03,590
[groans, whoops]

424
00:23:03,673 --> 00:23:04,800
[in English] Get out of here.

425
00:23:04,883 --> 00:23:07,177
[in English] Get out. Go!

426
00:23:07,260 --> 00:23:08,762
[in English] Stand up and let us fight.

427
00:23:08,845 --> 00:23:11,389
- [tense music playing]
- [grunts]

428
00:23:13,975 --> 00:23:15,560
[in English] Yes, yes.

429
00:23:15,644 --> 00:23:18,522
[in English] Now, we will fight
and see who the tough guy is.

430
00:23:18,605 --> 00:23:22,776
[in English] But remember, if you lose,

431
00:23:22,859 --> 00:23:26,321
I will cut her finger.

432
00:23:38,792 --> 00:23:41,378
[electronic blipping]

433
00:23:43,046 --> 00:23:45,799
[intense music playing]

434
00:23:49,594 --> 00:23:51,471
[Atoy] We won't be able
to get out anymore.

435
00:23:51,555 --> 00:23:53,682
We'll rot here.

436
00:23:53,765 --> 00:23:56,810
Think of the people who love you.

437
00:23:56,893 --> 00:23:59,020
No one cares about me now.

438
00:23:59,104 --> 00:24:00,981
[in English] Kill me now! Now.

439
00:24:01,064 --> 00:24:01,982
This is what you want, right?!

440
00:24:02,065 --> 00:24:03,275
[in English] You're not worth it.

441
00:24:03,358 --> 00:24:04,234
‪UP NEXT

442
00:24:04,317 --> 00:24:05,819
- [Red] <i>You will die!</i>
- [gunshot]

443
00:24:05,902 --> 00:24:07,404
You shouldn't give up.

444
00:24:07,487 --> 00:24:10,991
[Lily] <i>Surely, you left a mark</i>
<i>on at least one person.</i>

445
00:24:11,074 --> 00:24:12,409
[in English] Let's go, coward.

446
00:24:12,492 --> 00:24:13,618
[in English] I'll let you hit me first.

447
00:24:13,702 --> 00:24:15,412
[in English] You need this one.

448
00:24:15,495 --> 00:24:16,746
[grunts]

449
00:24:16,830 --> 00:24:20,000
I forgot you're a demon!

450
00:24:20,083 --> 00:24:21,835
Where is my real child?!

451
00:24:21,918 --> 00:24:24,629
I'll never tell you, even if you shoot me.

452
00:24:24,713 --> 00:24:26,298
- [grunts]
- [shouts]

453
00:24:27,048 --> 00:24:30,385
[grunting]

454
00:24:31,136 --> 00:24:32,179
[grunting and groaning]

455
00:24:32,262 --> 00:24:33,388
[clanging and clattering]

456
00:24:33,471 --> 00:24:35,432
- ["Mr. Tailor" playing]
- [grunts]

457
00:24:35,515 --> 00:24:36,850
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

458
00:24:36,933 --> 00:24:39,186
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

459
00:24:39,269 --> 00:24:42,606
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

460
00:24:42,689 --> 00:24:44,107
♪ Fix it ♪

461
00:24:44,191 --> 00:24:46,109
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
